  "description": "Make every ride your best ride.\n\nGeometry that works as hard as you do.\n\nEvery trail is different, and Wire Peak doesn't make you choose. Independently adjustable High/Low and Long/Short settings let you fine-tune the bike's character without giving anything else up. Low / Long — stable, plow-friendly, confident at speed. High / Short — poppy, playful, quick to change direction.\n\nAvinox M2S Drive Unit\n\nChoose between Class 1 or Class 3\n\nThe Wire Peak lets you switch seamlessly between Class 1 (pedal-assist up to 20 mph) and Class 3 (up to 28 mph). Crank it up to Class 3 via the companion app or display to fly down the road to the trailhead, then drop back to Class 1 to stay fully compliant on local trails.*Changing your e-bike from Class 1 to Class 3 may affect where it can legally be ridden. Riders are responsible for understanding and following all applicable local laws and regulations.\n\nSpec'd for the real world.\n\nBigger brakes, bigger rotors — because e-bike speeds need e-bike stopping power\n\ne-MTB-specific components throughout — rated for the added weight and torque of motor assist, not repurposed from an acoustic bike's parts bin\n\nBurlier suspension tune — matched to the higher average speeds an e-bike carries into rough terrain\n\nHeavier-duty tires — for the traction and puncture resistance big days actually demand",
